Feature: What each primitive does
  Each [[agent plan]] has one [[primitive]]. The primitive tells the plane how to fly: to a
  point, round a point, in a height band, after another aircraft or away from it. The plane
  holds each primitive until a new plan comes or the plan runs out.

  The points of the plans are latitude and longitude, with the altitude above [[home]]. The
  console of the runner takes metres north and east of home, and changes them for you. The
  plane moves a circle in from the [[fence]] if the whole circle does not fit inside it.

  We measured the distances and the heights on this page in a simulation of the T1-S that uses
  the same [[executor]]. The plane starts at 30 m over the [[arena centre]], to the north, at
  15 m/s. The console does not show these distances and heights. In the simulation, the other aircraft is a model
  plane too.

  The other aircraft come from [[track]]s. The ground sends each one as an `ADSB_VEHICLE`
  message. The low byte of its ICAO address is the id that a plan names as its target. The
  plane ignores a track that it has not heard for 3 s. In the runner, the ids of the planes
  are 1 for Kestrel, 2 for Merlin and 3 for Swift. After the game, the console sends the tracks
  of Merlin and Swift to Kestrel twice a second. Type `silent` to stop them, and `heard` to send
  them again.

  Expectation: Go to flies over the point, then circles it
    The plane flies straight to the point. When it is over the point, it circles the point at
    the [[loiter]] radius, about 35 m for the T1-S. It holds the height of the plan.

    Given the reported primitive is go to
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s
    When the plane flies on for 2 minutes
    Then the closest approach to the point is at most 10 m
    And the greatest distance from the point in the last minute is at most 45 m
    And the lowest height in the last minute is at least 38 m
    And the highest height in the last minute is at most 42 m

  Expectation: An orbit plan circles a point
    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    When the ground sends an orbit plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is orbit
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s

  Expectation: Orbit holds its radius and its height
    The plane circles the point at the radius of the plan, in the direction that it already
    turns. A radius that is too small for the plane becomes the smallest circle that it can fly.

    Given the reported primitive is orbit
    When the plane flies on for 2 minutes
    Then the least distance from the point in the last minute is at least 40 m
    And the greatest distance from the point in the last minute is at most 50 m
    And the lowest height in the last minute is at least 43 m
    And the highest height in the last minute is at most 47 m

  Expectation: A band plan holds a height band
    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    When the ground sends a band plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is band
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s

  Expectation: Band keeps the plane between its two heights
    The altitude of a band plan is the bottom of the band, and its radius is the thickness of
    the band. The plane climbs or sinks into the band. Then it circles over the arena, inside
    the fence. In [[tag]], each plane has its own band, so that two planes do not meet by chance.

    Given the reported primitive is band
    When the plane flies on for 2 minutes
    Then the lowest height in the last minute is at least 34 m
    And the highest height in the last minute is at most 46 m
    And the farthest distance from the arena centre is at most 85 m

  Expectation: A loiter plan circles where the plane is
    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    When the ground sends a loiter plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is loiter
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s

  Expectation: Loiter stays round the place where it began
    The plane circles the place where it got the plan, at the loiter radius and at its height.
    Near the fence, the circle moves in until it fits.

    Given the reported primitive is loiter
    When the plane flies on for 2 minutes
    Then the least distance from the point in the last minute is at least 25 m
    And the greatest distance from the point in the last minute is at most 45 m

  Expectation: A pursue plan chases another aircraft
    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    And the other aircraft is round the arena
    When the ground sends a pursue plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is pursue
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s

  Expectation: Pursue closes on the target and stays on its tail
    The plane flies to the place where the target will be, and it matches the speed of the
    target. It stays just outside the [[separation]] zone, behind the target. Then the target
    cannot turn away from it easily.

    Given the reported primitive is pursue
    And the other aircraft is round the arena
    When the plane flies on for 2 minutes
    Then the greatest distance from the other aircraft in the last minute is at most 25 m
    And the closest distance to the other aircraft is above 4 m

  Expectation: An evade plan breaks away from another aircraft
    Given the flight mode of the plane is AGENT
    And the other aircraft is after your plane
    When the ground sends an evade plan
    Then the reply to the plan is accepted
    And the reported plan goes up by 1
    And the reported primitive is evade
    And the time to live of the plan is 600 s

  Expectation: Evade opens the distance from a chaser
    The plane turns away from the other aircraft and flies fast, 20 m above or below it. Near the edge
    of the arena, it turns back in, so that it does not fly out.

    Given the reported primitive is evade
    And the other aircraft is after your plane
    When the plane flies on for 10 seconds
    Then the distance to the other aircraft is at least 35 m

  Expectation: A target that goes silent ends the chase
    If the plane does not hear its target for 3 s, it cannot chase it or break away from it.
    It circles where it is, as for a plan that runs out.

    Given the reported primitive is pursue
    When the track of the other aircraft is not heard
    And the plane flies on for 5 seconds
    Then the reported fallback is plan expired
